=========================================================================

bstore is object storage as a market on the BSV blockchain's overlay
hosts. A writer publishes an object once, as a CHIRP closure, with a
signed entry on its bucket's records topic; storage providers receive
the same bytes, advertise what they hold with UHRP advertisements, and
race for a hold bounty paid by rank to the first that pass a possession
challenge. A bucket's owner keeps a chain of mined tokens committing to
the whole key map, so a reader proves what a key names, that a key is
absent and that a listing page is complete. Readers speak S3 through a
gateway that verifies every byte before it is sent.

